2026-09-25 M2 review R3-F1: a filer with no 10-K yet gets its fiscal years from its 10-Qs' year-to-date periods (6- and 9-month starts; with only first-quarter reports, the 3-month starts), each ending the day before the next; the last is open. A quarter never reported ends the day before the next quarter's 3-month period, so a year without its Q1 (an IPO listed mid-year) keeps its 3-month Q2. GE Vernova's 2024 quarters are written as each 10-Q is filed (7,260M, 8,204M, 8,913M), not back-dated at its first 10-K. Every column is set for every quarter end, so a quarter end learned later adds no empty version.
